name=[B42.20] Auto All - Cook, Read, Clean, Sterilize, Rip, Tailoring, Mechanics, Reload & Dismantle
id=AutoAll
description=Nine quality of life automations in one client side mod for Build 42.20.
description=Auto Cook: right click a pot, bowl or pan and let the character fill the meal with the best ingredients on its own, spreading the food types so the dish does not make you unhappy. The Auto Cook... entry opens a window where you pick the dish, set how much of each ingredient goes in, and say whether the meal is for calories, for hunger, for balance or for losing weight.
description=Auto Read: right click any book and the character reads every skill book and recipe magazine within reach, skipping the ones above or below its level, and puts each one back.
description=Auto Clean: one option on any sink, toilet, bath, rain collector, barrel or well washes you, your clothes, your gear and your dirty bandages in one go, with or without cleaning products, then wrings the clothes out and puts them back on.
description=Auto Sterilize: sterilize every bandage or every rag in one click, from your inventory or straight out of a container, using the alcohol or boiled water in reach.
description=Auto Rip: turn a looted wardrobe into ripped sheets, denim strips and leather strips in one batch. Worn, held and favourite items are never touched, and the strips go back to the container the clothing came from.
description=Auto Dismantle: right click any electronic - watches, alarm clocks, radios, walkie talkies, CD players, headphones, torches, remotes - and take every one you have apart in a single batch for Electrical XP. The screwdriver is picked up once, not once per item.
description=Auto Repair: find every hole in everything within reach, worn clothing included, and sew them all shut. Picks the fabric that fully restores the part when you have it.
description=Train Tailoring: one button on the clothing inspection window patches every body part and unpicks the patches again, over and over, until you run out of materials or tell it to stop.
description=Auto Mechanics: two entries on the vehicle mechanics window strip a car of every part it will give up, or fit every part you are carrying, one at a time. Parts the game does not give a sure thing on are skipped rather than gambled with.
description=Train Reload: right click a magazine or a firearm and the character loads and unloads it in a loop until you move or press ESC.
description=Every automation queues its work in batches of vanilla timed actions, so XP, animations, sounds and multiplayer sync are the base game's, and single player can fast forward straight through the job.
description=Auto Medicine: right click any body part in the Health window and the character treats every wound in one go - bullets and glass out, burns washed, wounds disinfected and bandaged, a sterilised bandage first when you have one.
description=Auto Exercise: the Muscle Manager loop, built in. Tick AUTO on the vanilla Fitness panel and the character trains, rests when endurance runs out and starts the next set on its own, eating and treating pain from nearby bags if it needs to.
description=Auto VHS: right click any tape and the character watches every recording within reach that still teaches something, then takes it back out.
description=Auto Open: right click a sealed tin or a preserved jar and the character opens every one within reach, fetching them out of containers and picking the can opener up only once. The opened food goes back where the sealed one came from.
